3 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":127791,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":12683,"text":"<p>Simplify the statement $\\neg (\\neg P) \\lor \\neg (\\neg Q).$</p>\n","choice1":"$P \\lor Q$","choice2":"$P \\lor \\neg Q$","choice3":"$P \\land Q$","choice4":"$\\neg P \\land \\neg Q$","choice5":"$\\neg  P \\land Q$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Two negations in a row cancel each other out, so:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>we can simplify $\\neg (\\neg P)$ to $P ,$ and </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>we can also simplify  $\\neg (\\neg Q)$ to $Q.$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the given statement can be simplified to </p>\n<p>\\[\nP \\lor Q.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"example":{"id":12683,"title":"Simplifying a Double Negation"},"group":{"id":24088,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251832,"answer":{"id":62347836,"cread":"2026-10-16T08:43:26.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":10923},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62347898,"created":"2026-10-16T08:43:43.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12563,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 8:43 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":176862,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":12681,"text":"<blockquote>\n<p>$3$ is an integer number, and $\\sqrt{3}$ is <strong>not</strong> a rational number.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$3$ is an integer number}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$Q: \\textrm{$\\sqrt{3}$ is a rational number}$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","choice1":"$P \\land \\neg Q$","choice2":"$\\neg P \\lor \\neg Q$","choice3":"$\\neg (P \\land Q)$","choice4":"$\\neg P \\land Q$","choice5":"$P \\lor \\neg Q$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>The negation is represented by the symbol &quot;$\\neg$&quot;.</p>\n<p>The sentence</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$3$ is an integer number</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>can be expressed symbolically as $P.$ </p>\n<p>The sentence</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$\\sqrt{3}$ is <strong>not</strong> a rational number</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>can be expressed symbolically as $\\neg Q.$</p>\n<p>Therefore, the sentence</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$3$ is an integer number, and $\\sqrt{3}$ is <strong>not</strong> a rational number</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>can be expressed symbolically as $P \\land \\neg Q.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"example":{"id":12681,"title":"Expressing a Negated Sentence in Symbolic Form"},"group":{"id":24444,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251832,"answer":{"id":62347898,"cread":"2026-10-16T08:43:43.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12563},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62348061,"created":"2026-10-16T08:44:20.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[0,0,0,0]","timeElapsed":32477,"number":5,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 8:44 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:32","question":{"id":182395,"format":"SS","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12682,"text":"<p> Find the missing values in the following truth table:</p>\n","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p><p>First, we add a column for $\\neg B, $ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column for $B.$</p></p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, \\neg B\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p><p>Then, we add a column for $A \\land \\neg B.$ Remember that $A \\land \\neg B$ is true if both $\\neg B$ and $A$ are true.</p></p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, \\neg B\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,A \\land \\neg B\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n\n<p><p>Finally, 